      "message": "Gemini review:\n\n* **Deadlock Potential on Assertion Failure:**\n    In `test_lock_flash_control_register`, you acquire a lock using `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(1)` and release it at the end of the test. \n    Zephyr\u0027s `zassert_*` macros are designed to abort the current test immediately upon failure (typically via a `return` or `longjmp`). If any of the `zassert_*` checks fail, the execution will exit the function *without* calling `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(0)`. \n    Consequently, the flash storage remains locked. When the test suite finishes and calls `flash_physical_after()`, it will attempt to call `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(1)` again, which will likely cause a deadlock and hang the entire test runner.\n    **Recommendation:** Move the lock acquisition and release to ZTEST fixture setup/teardown hooks (e.g., a test-specific `before` and `after` function using `ZTEST_FIXTURE`), or ensure cleanup runs safely. Alternatively, use `zexpect_*` macros (if available in your Zephyr version) which do not abort execution on failure, though a fixture `after` hook is the most robust way to guarantee the lock is released.",
      "revId": "620d78a5c65ea0b0771057601b5f6094fdea91aa",
